From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: create defaults for reloaded radios

Per-radio metrics and steering defaults were created only in put_radio()'s
new-radio branch.  When a radio was already present in the controller model,
pradio was found but dm remained NULL and the complete policy initialization
block was skipped.  A cold controller reconstruction consequently exposed
three radio-metrics rows for the colocated agent and none for four otherwise
complete extenders.  No network-wide Policy Configuration Request could then
be constructed, leaving every associated STA RCPI at zero.

Resolve the owning data model after updating either a new or existing radio.
The existing per-radio duplicate checks keep this idempotent while allowing a
reloaded radio to repair missing defaults with its real device and radio IDs.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
---
 src/dm/dm_easy_mesh_list.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dm/dm_easy_mesh_list.cpp b/src/dm/dm_easy_mesh_list.cpp
--- a/src/dm/dm_easy_mesh_list.cpp
+++ b/src/dm/dm_easy_mesh_list.cpp
@@ -373,6 +373,11 @@ void dm_easy_mesh_list_t::put_radio(const char *key, const dm_radio_t *radio)
     }
     *pradio = *radio;
 
+    // Existing radios also need an owning model so a controller reload can
+    // repair policy defaults that were absent from persistent state.
+    if (dm == NULL) {
+        dm = get_data_model(pradio->m_radio_info.id.net_id, pradio->m_radio_info.id.dev_mac);
+    }
     // Create default per-radio policies (radio_metrics_rep and steering_param) for newly discovered radios.
     if (dm != NULL) {
         bool has_radio_metrics = false, has_steering_param = false;
